Safe — copy par iterate karo:

t = {1, 2, 3}
for x in list(t):
    t.add(x + 10)
print('copy par iterate safe:', sorted(t))
# copy par iterate safe: [1, 2, 3, 11, 12, 13]

user_roles = {'editor', 'viewer'}
required = {'admin'}
print('admin allowed?', required.issubset(user_roles))
# admin allowed? False
print('missing:', required - user_roles)
# missing: {'admin'}

candidate_skills = {'python', 'sql', 'git'}
job_skills = {'python', 'sql', 'docker', 'aws'}
print('matched:', candidate_skills & job_skills)
# matched: {'sql', 'python'}
print('gaps:', job_skills - candidate_skills)
# gaps: {'aws', 'docker'}
print('match %:', round(100 * len(candidate_skills & job_skills) / len(job_skills)))
# match %: 50

s = {1, 2, 3}
try:
    for x in s:
        s.discard(x)
except RuntimeError as e:
    print('RuntimeError:', e)
# RuntimeError: Set changed size during iteration

Kyun: iterator set ke current size/state par depend karta hai. Beech me size badalne se iteration ka behaviour undefined ho jata, isliye Python fail-fast karta hai (dict ke saath bhi same).

Fix:

# 1) copy par iterate karo (mutate original)
t = {1, 2, 3}
for x in list(t):
    t.add(x + 10)
print(sorted(t))
# [1, 2, 3, 11, 12, 13]

# 2) comprehension se naya set banao (sabse clean)
s = {x for x in s if x % 2}

# 3) difference_update/intersection_update bulk ke liye (atomic, iterate nahi karta)
s.difference_update(expired)

# 4) pending deletions collect karke baad me apply kar do

Dhyan: `s.discard(x)` ke saath `for x in s` kabhi mat likhna — agar aap sirf KHAALI karna chahte ho to `s.clear()` ek hi call me kaam kar deta hai.

Rule: mutate aur iterate ek saath nahi — ya copy par iterate karo (`list(s)`), ya naya collection build karo (comprehension), ya bulk API (`difference_update`) use karo.

candidate_skills = {'python', 'sql', 'git'}
job_skills = {'python', 'sql', 'docker', 'aws'}
print('matched:', candidate_skills & job_skills)
# matched: {'sql', 'python'}
print('gaps:', job_skills - candidate_skills)
# gaps: {'aws', 'docker'}
print('match %:', round(100 * len(candidate_skills & job_skills) / len(job_skills)))
# match %: 50
